WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.810
- Beauty products have
been around forever,

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.610
but how long?

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.240
How did it all start?

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.870
For example, the red lip.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.960
What is the origin and history

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.570
of one of beauty's most
important products?

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:15.820
I love this, take a look.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.203
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.105 --> 00:00:23.840
The history of red
lipstick can be traced back

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.050
almost 5,000 years.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.000
Ancient Sumerians made
the world's first lipstick

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.170
out of crushed gemstones and white lead.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.210
Rumor has it that Egyptian
Pharaoh, Cleopatra

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.950
made hers from flowers, fish
scales and crushed ants.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.870
That gives a new meaning
to all natural ingredients,

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:42.703
doesn't it?

00:00:42.703 --> 00:00:44.780
Elizabeth the First
believed that a red lip

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.870
had magical powers to
heal and ward off danger,

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.070
which is darkly ironic since
most lipstick and makeups

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.520
were made of poisonous lead.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.280
Flash forward to the early 20th century

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:01.000
when a bold red lip was seen as shocking.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.100
In New York City, suffragettes
took to the streets,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.800
campaigning for the vote,

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.560
wearing a red lip to
symbolize the new woman.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.360
In the 30s, Vogue declared
lipstick the most important

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.490
cosmetics for women and sales skyrocketed.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:16.800
During World War II,

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.860
a red lip became the symbol of patriotism

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.470
and feminine resilience.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.620
The US government ordered
war factory dressing rooms

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.120
to be stocked with lipstick
to boost female workers'

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.830
efficiency and morale.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.270
That's my kind of government mandate.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:35.930
Today. the red lips is still
seen as a symbol of power,

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.780
sexiness and feminine rebellion.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.637
As Coco Chanel once said,

00:01:40.637 --> 00:01:44.877
"If you are sad, add more
lipstick and attack."

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.215
Well, that's a lot of history for a little

00:01:49.215 --> 00:01:50.230
(kisses)

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.350
rouge on the lips?

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:54.650
Okay, now what do you need
to execute this iconic,

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.910
iconic beauty look?

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.520
Okay, it's really quite simple.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.130
You need a good lip liner,

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.980
especially when you get a little older.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:03.900
That's right.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.900
It really brings out your
inner ReeRee or Marilyn.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.840
I didn't need lip liner when I was younger

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.860
but now I certainly do.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.120
And this lip liner is by Lip Bar

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.460
and this is a fantastic
lip liner right here,

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.620
like highly recommended.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.460
And so I'm gonna just do
my lip liner real quick.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.000
And then I think one of the biggest

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.150
and most important reds in
the history of red lipstick

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.400
is the Mac Russian Red.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.740
This is the one that Madonna made popular

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.230
in the 90s and you could not get it.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.910
It was completely sold out everywhere.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:50.260
So I hold this as the
benchmark to all red lipsticks.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.630
Now I'm going to put on a Flower Beauty.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.563
This component is really cool
'cause it's double ended.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.470
Uh-huh and this is called Red Velvet

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.753
because it reminds me of cake.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.193
Uh-huh, thank you, Arturo.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:11.420
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.253
Mm hmm.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.690
And what's really cool
is the other component

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.793
has a little lip gloss on the other side.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.847
It's funny.

00:03:23.847 --> 00:03:24.880
You know, when women put on a red lip,

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.760
it like changes their demeanor
and some people call it

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.700
the high heel of makeup.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.300
So if there's a little tool that you have

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.260
that can change your demeanor

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.970
and have a little light bulb in your face,

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.670
then I say, turn on the red light.

00:03:42.119 --> 00:03:44.702
(upbeat music)

